<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly steady on Monday, reflecting the stable rates in the money market, traders said.</p>
<p>The two-week and one-month rates, however, were sligthly up due to higher demand for pesos to tide banks over the New Year holidays, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Those are the only maturities that are moving,&quot; said a foreign bank dealer.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 DEC 16		  DEC 13</p>
<p>    1 W		11  1/16		11  1/16</p>
<p>    2 W		11  3/16		11  1/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/8		 11  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/8		 11  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		11  3/16		11  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  5/16		11  5/16</p>
<p>    12M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    VAL		17-Dec		  16-Dec</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
